  "body_html": "<h1>Nature In Extensive Games</h1>\n<p>An extensive game with Nature has chance nodes at which no strategic player\nchooses an action. Instead, the game description specifies a probability\ndistribution over successors. A strategy profile of the strategic players then\ninduces a probability distribution over terminal outcomes.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Section 6.2.5] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>. Nature or hazard player chooses successors according to specified probability distributions.</li>\n</ul>",
